# Apple provisioning profiles are account-scoped signing material: the owner
# drops ESExtension/plugsight-esext.provisionprofile (or points PLUGSIGHT_ES_PROFILE
# at one) for the ES release; it must never be committed or reach the OSS mirror
# (docs/RELEASE-ES-RUNBOOK.md). The OSS denylist backstops this too.
*.provisionprofile
*.mobileprovision

# Private owner credential/setup steps (never committed, and denied by the OSS
# mirror allowlist so they are never published to the public repo)
OWNER-SETUP.md

# Session build-overview (private, not product source)
plugsight-v1-build-overview.html

# Throwaway design variant explorations (not shipped)
.variants/

# Claude Code local state (kaizen fixers create worktrees under .claude/worktrees/)
.claude/
